meta {
  name: List Radiology Tests (Listing & Views)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/radiology-tests/listing?view=DEFAULT&page=1&limit=20&search=CT
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  view: DEFAULT
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  search: CT
  ~modality: CT
  ~departmentId:
  ~categoryId:
  ~subCategoryId:
  ~status: ACTIVE
  ~sortBy: priceMsrp
  ~sortOrder: -1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  masterDataId: 2db13b5e-4a25-412f-bcd9-68bcbeea9d59
}

docs {
  Configurable listing screen for a master data's radiology tests. One endpoint;
  the `view` query param selects which columns are projected. Paginated **by
  radiology test**. Business JWT. 404 `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND` if the parent master
  data is missing/other tenant.

  ## Search & filters (all optional)

  - `search` — matches `testName` OR `testCode` only (case-insensitive).
  - `modality` — XRAY|CT|MRI|ULTRASOUND|MAMMOGRAPHY|PET|FLUOROSCOPY|DEXA|OTHER.
  - `departmentId` / `categoryId` / `subCategoryId` — filter by id (the matching
    **names** are resolved server-side for the views that show them; the flat
    model has no Prisma relation, so `departmentName` is an in-memory resolve and
    is intentionally **not** sortable).
  - `status` — `ACTIVE` | `INACTIVE` (maps to `isActive`). Soft-deleted tests are
    always excluded.
  - `page` / `limit` — standard pagination (limit capped at 100).

  ## Sorting (applied before pagination)

  - `sortBy` + `sortOrder` — `sortOrder` is `1` (asc) or `-1` (desc). Omit both
    for the default (`createdAt desc`). An unsupported `sortBy` → 400
    `VALIDATION_ERROR` (allowlisted server-side).
  - Allowed `sortBy` keys: `testName`, `testCode`, `aka`, `modality`, `bodyPart`,
    `icdCode`, `loincCode`, `samplePriorityType`, `priceMsrp`, `priceMinimum`,
    `priceMaximum`, `priceOriginal`, `franchisePrice`, `emergencyPrice`,
    `discountCapPct`, `tatMinValue`, `tatMaxValue`, `isAllowPriceOverride`,
    `isAllowDiscounts`, `isHideInOrderScreen`, `isEnableCms`, `isPreferenceTest`,
    `usefulFor`, `isActive`.

  ## Views (`view`)

  `DEFAULT` (default), `BASIC_DETAILS`, `PRICING`, `TAT`, `FLAGS`, `NOTES`,
  `OVERVIEW`. Unlike lab tests the flat radiology model has **no child-centric
  views** (`SAMPLE`/`RESULTS`/`REFERENCE_*`) — radiology tests carry no samples or
  result parameters. Don't send an empty `view` (an empty enum → 400
  `VALIDATION_ERROR`); omit it to get `DEFAULT`.

  > The disabled (`~`) query params above are examples — enable the ones you want.
}
